From: q706f port <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: q706f: keep the ADSP fastrpc remote heap out of CMA

sm8250.dtsi declares adsp-rpc-remote-heap as a reusable shared-dma-pool and
the fastrpc ADSP node assigns the whole region to LPASS + ADSP_HEAP at probe,
removing HLOS access. Reusable CMA pages are still handed out to movable
allocations, so once memory fills (Flatpak installs, browser video) Linux
writes to pages that the hypervisor no longer maps for HLOS. The TZ diag log
shows SGIFatal (same codes every time) on a random CPU and the SoC resets via
PS_HOLD with no kernel message. Make the region no-map (stock keeps every
remote heap static as well).

Tested 23.11.2026 (RAM boot, runtime DTB edit): CMA fully used, GNOME Web and
GNOME Software running, no reset; before, the same load reset within 1-3 min.
See docs/cercetare-tz-sgifatal-2026-11-23/.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts	2026-11-23 22:05:34.276211523 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts	2026-11-23 22:05:34.282029220 +0200
@@ -328,6 +328,18 @@
 };
 
 
+/*
+ * fastrpc hands this heap to the ADSP at probe (qcom_scm_assign_mem: HLOS ->
+ * LPASS + ADSP_HEAP). As a "reusable" CMA region its pages are also lent to
+ * Linux movable allocations, so under memory pressure the kernel touches pages
+ * it no longer owns and the secure side declares a fatal error (TZ SGIFatal,
+ * PS_HOLD reset). Keep it out of the page allocator.
+ */
+&adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem {
+	/delete-property/ reusable;
+	no-map;
+};
+
 &adsp {
 	status = "okay";
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8250/q706f/adsp.mbn";
